  "question": {
    "text": "The distance between object and its <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> times magnified virtual image as produced by a convex lens is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The focal length of the lens used is ________ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi><mo>.</mo></math>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "15",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0073_0995d695ff71.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 157px;\"/></p><p>The image will be formed on the same side as the object. Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>u</mi></math></p><p>Given: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>–</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math> (-ve sign as the object is real)</p><p>From lens formula, we can write </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>f</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p>"
  }
}